    "question": "What protections apply to a privileged administrator who works remotely?",
    "top_score": 0.41720762495714286,
    "top_vector_score": 0.534786403,
    "top_keyword_score": 0.14285714285714285,
    "top_section": "REMOTE WORK POLICY",
    "retrieval_seconds": 1.1208543879911304,
    "answer_seconds": 6.331538001002627,
    "total_seconds": 7.4524222549953265,
    "answer": "No separate protection is specified for remote privileged administrators. The following safeguards apply:\n\n- Privileged admin/root access requires MFA, follows least privilege, is reviewed and recertified quarterly, and must use individual, auditable accounts rather than shared accounts.\n- Data in transit must use TLS 1.2 or higher; data at rest must use AES-256; and the laptop must have full-disk encryption enabled. (Information Security Policy)\n- Sensitive data cannot be stored on personal devices, and security controls such as VPN or endpoint protection cannot be bypassed or disabled. (Acceptable Use Policy)\n- The remote workspace must be safe, ergonomic, and distraction-free. Working outside the employee\u2019s country of employment requires prior written approval from HR and Legal. (Remote Work Policy)",
